[170.816467, "o", "    ✓ todo — 8/8 done\r\n  ⚙ task \r\n    ✓ task implementor — 39 tool call(s)\r\n  deepseek-v4.1-flash — 10 tool call(s) so far\r\n## What's wrong\r\n\r\nYour PATH resolves `python`/`python3`/`pip3` to a **source-built Python 3.13.1 at `/usr/local`**, and that interpreter has **no `pip` module at all**. The `pip3` launcher script is still there on disk but points at a module that isn't installed:\r\n\r\n```\r\n$ pip3 --version\r\nTraceback (most recent call last):\r\n  File \"/usr/local/bin/pip3\", line 5, in <module>\r\n    from pip._internal.cli.main import main\r\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'pip'\r\n\r\n$ python3 -m pip --version\r\n/usr/local/bin/python3: No module named pip\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe launcher is `#!/usr/local/bin/python3.13` — so it's not a PATH-stacking or \"wrong venv\" problem, and there's no `VIRTUAL_ENV`, `PYTHONPATH`, `PYTHONHOME`, `PIP_*` variable or any `pip.conf` (`/etc/pip.conf`, `~/.pip/pip.conf`, `~/.config/pip/pip.conf` all absent) interfering. The module is simply gone.\r\n\r\n## The red herring\r\n\r\nTher"]
[170.816545, "o", "e is a **second** Python: Debian 12's `/usr/lib/python3.11`, which carries a PEP 668 `EXTERNALLY-MANAGED` marker and will refuse installs with `externally-managed-environment`. That is normal and expected, and it is **not** what you're hitting — `/usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages` has no `EXTERNALLY-MANAGED` file and is writable (you're `root`, `drwxr-xr-x root:root`). If you'd been on `python3.11` you'd get the PEP 668 error text; instead you get a `ModuleNotFoundError`, which is a different (and more basic) breakage.\r\n\r\n## The fix\r\n\r\nThe bundled bootstrap is present and needs no network — `python3 -m ensurepip --version` reports `pip 24.3.1`, so:\r\n\r\n```sh\r\npython3 -m ensurepip --upgrade\r\n```\r\n\r\nThat restores the `pip` module and repairs the existing `/usr/local/bin/pip3` launcher. Afterwards, prefer `python3 -m venv .venv` for project work rather than installing into `/usr/local` — `venv`/`ensurepip` are both available on this build, so that works offline too.\r\n\r\n## What I did and did not do\r\n\r\n"]
[170.816553, "o", "I ran read-only inspection only — version queries, config lookups, `ls`, `test -w`, and `pip install --dry-run` (which never reached pip, since the module is missing). **I did not run `ensurepip`, install anything, or modify the host interpreter.** That container is root-owned and sits outside this repository, and stripping pip from `/usr/local` is, in some base images, deliberate — so changing it unattended isn't mine to decide. The command above is the whole fix; run it and `python3 -m pip --version` should answer cleanly.\r\n\r\n[result] role=coordinator model=deepseek-v4.1-flash tools=10 surface=b21887234a3d\r\n"]
